{"name":"Black Magic","hex":"#4f4554","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black magic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Magic derived from evil forces, as distinct from good or benign forces; or magic performed with the intention of doing harm.","A technology, process, etc., that is mysterious, esoteric; anything which appears to be almost magic to those who do not understand it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_magic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black magic","blocks":[{"text":"Black magic, sometimes dark magic, traditionally refers to the use of magic or supernatural powers for evil and selfish purposes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_magic","wikidata":"Q690768"},{"title":"Black Magic (Little Mix song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Black Magic\" is a song recorded by British girl group Little Mix, released in May 2015 through Syco Music and Columbia Records as the lead single from their third studio album, Get Weird (2015). It is a teen pop and dance pop song with influences of '80s pop music. The single received acclaim from music critics upon release, who praised it for its catchy sound and upbeat tempo, and comparisons were made with the songs from the group's debut album, DNA (2012)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/Little_Mix_-_Black_Magic_%28Official_Single_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Magic_(Little_Mix_song)","wikidata":"Q20012173"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeptameron_magic_circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Sprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Sprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Sprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff/lossy-page1-1280px-Sprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Sprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Sprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Malleus Maleficarum, 1669 edition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASprenger_-_Malleus_maleficarum%2C_1669_-_BEIC_9477645.tiff"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Vudu.jpg/500px-Vudu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_